# API architecture

Follow existing modules under `apps/api/src/module/{master|core|meta}/{domain}/`.

## Layering

```
Controller → executeMethod → Service → Repo → Prisma
                ↓
         ResponseBuilder
```

- Controllers extend `BaseController` and return `ResponseVm` via `executeMethod` only (no direct `ResponseBuilder` / raw returns).
- Services extend `BaseService`; business rules and NotFound/Conflict live here.
- Repos extend `BaseRepo`; audit + soft delete live here. Do not query Prisma from controllers or services when a repo method exists.
- Every domain HTTP route must go through this stack (see always-on rule `base-layer-ethics.mdc`).
- Wire `MODULE_CONFIG` with `loadModuleConfig(__dirname)` and keep `config/module.yml`.
- DTOs: `create-*.dto.ts` + `update-*.dto.ts` (`PartialType` from `@nestjs/mapped-types`). Validate with `class-validator`.

## CRUD

- `POST /` create · `GET /` list · `GET /:id` (static routes like `slug/:slug`, `code/:code`, `summary` **before** `:id`) · `PATCH /:id` · `DELETE /:id` soft-delete (`isDeleted: true`).
- No hard deletes for domain CRUD.

## UTC dates

- Use `utcNow` / `toUtcDate` / `optionalUtcDate` / `toUtcIso` / `isWithinUtcWindow` from `common/utility/date.utility.ts`.
- Never invent local-timezone date helpers. Persist `DateTime` as timestamptz; assume UTC everywhere.
- `BaseRepo` already stamps `createdAt` / `updatedAt`; use the same UTC helpers in nested creates.

## Utilities placement

- Cross-cutting → `apps/api/src/common/utility/`
- Domain-only → `apps/api/src/module/.../{domain}/utility/`
- Do not dump one-off helpers into services when they belong in `utility/`.

## Responses

Use `ResponseBuilder` statuses only: success `200`, warning `401`, authError `403`, codeError `1000`.

## Example shape

```
module/master/address/
  address.controller.ts
  address.service.ts
  address.repo.ts
  address.module.ts
  dto/
  utility/
  config/module.yml
```
